 "Incumbent Vicente Gonzalez (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Vicente Gonzalez, the Democratic incumbent, faces Republican Eric Flores in a South Texas district that leans Republican by about three points. Gonzalez holds a clear financial advantage, with $2.5 million on hand compared to Flores's $686,000, though Flores has raised a substantial $2.9 million and drawn outside Republican support. Most expert raters place the race at Lean D, with two calling it a Tossup, and prediction markets price the Democrat's chances in the low 80s. The only recent independent poll, from August, showed Gonzalez up three points. National Republicans have invested heavily here, with Trump and Vance holding rallies in the region, underscoring the seat's importance for House control. Gonzalez's incumbency and fundraising edge give him the advantage, but the district's lean and the GOP's commitment keep the race within reach for Flores.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7969, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7826, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7895, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8125, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7373, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7369, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7694, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7446, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8106, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7774, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7834, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7562, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7186, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7472, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7411, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7622, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7079, "margin": 4.0}]}